From: local private research
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi_osal: Inline init_dummy_netdev() setup on 6.16+

6.16 turned init_dummy_netdev() into a static helper in net/core/dev.c and
removed the export, so the call in mt_init_dummy_netdev() has neither a
prototype nor a symbol to link against:

  mt_osal_net.c:673:2: error: implicit declaration of function
  'init_dummy_netdev' [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]

It only performs three setup steps, so do them here instead. Kernels
before 6.16 keep using the helper (void return since 6.9).

Signed-off-by: local private research
---
--- a/mt_osal_net.c
+++ b/mt_osal_net.c
@@ -669,7 +669,14 @@
 
 int mt_init_dummy_netdev(struct net_device *dev)
 {
-#if KERNEL_VERSION(6, 9, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE
+#if (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 16, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
+	/* 6.16 起 init_dummy_netdev() 收成了 net/core/dev.c 里的 static 函数，
+	 * 不再导出，模块既没有原型也没有符号可链。这里按它的实现做同样三步。 */
+	dev->reg_state = NETREG_DUMMY;
+	set_bit(__LINK_STATE_PRESENT, &dev->state);
+	set_bit(__LINK_STATE_START, &dev->state);
+	return 0;
+#elif KERNEL_VERSION(6, 9, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE
 	init_dummy_netdev(dev);
 	return 0;
 #else
